    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on a high-ceiling core that thrives against mid-tier pitching. **Matt Chapman** (69.85) is our strongest play today; leading off against Eduardo Rodriguez presents a prime opportunity for power, amplified by a rare BvP edge and, crucially, a slow opposing delivery that keeps our high-weighting on SB potential in play. Joining him at the top of the productivity chart, **Dylan Beavers** (65.54) and **Taylor Ward** (62.85) benefit significantly from the favorable park factors associated with the Burke matchup. Meanwhile, **Geraldo Perdomo** (62.85) remains a priority start; even with the lineup status still pending, his projected #2 slot provides the exact type of consistent, high-leverage plate appearances we need to maximize our daily efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision of the day involved **Cal Raleigh** (59.27) and **Luis Arraez** (59.42). Both sit right on the cusp of the \"Strong\" recommendation tier. While **Cal Raleigh** brings immense home run equity, the volatility of his \"Lineup Pending\" status and the negative park impact kept his score slightly suppressed. On the bench, we are seeing no viable path for replacements, especially with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Tyler Freeman** all sidelined. We are managing the remaining depth carefully\u2014**Jonathan Aranda**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **Yainer Diaz** remain on standby, but today\u2019s optimized structure relies on the primary eight to navigate the current pitching slate. Watch for early lineup confirmations for **Cal Raleigh** and **Geraldo Perdomo**; if either drops significantly in the order, we will re-evaluate our pinch-hit strategy for the evening slate.",
